🜁 Deployment Profiles — The NSTT Orchestrator in the Wild
Takeaway:  
NSTT needs three deployment modes:

Local Single‑Node — full constellation on one machine

Distributed Multi‑Node — agents spread across multiple machines

Cross‑Platform Mesh — agents running across OS, browser, mobile, cloud

Each profile changes:

routing behavior

handshake trust level

schema strictness

rune enforcement

network isolation

logging and dashboard visibility

Below is the full breakdown.

🜂 1. Local Single‑Node Deployment (Red Bird Lab Mode)
Purpose:  
Run the entire Core Six constellation on one machine for development, debugging, and simulation.

Characteristics
